  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OSCE Special Monitoring Mission 2015</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">OSSE Special Monitoring Mission 2015</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen syftar till att sekondera fyra observat&#xf6;rer fr&#xe5;n FBA till OSCE special monitoring mission i Ukraina. FBA har ansvar f&#xf6;r finansiell uppf&#xf6;ljning och rapportering av insatsen samt rekrytering och utbildning av observat&#xf6;rer inf&#xf6;r utresa. &#xd6;vergripande m&#xe5;l med insatsen &#xe4;r att &#xf6;ka stabiliteten och s&#xe4;kerheten i Ukraina baserad p&#xe5; respekt f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter. Insatsen &#xe4;r h&#xf6;gst relevant f&#xf6;r den r&#xe5;dande situationen och konflikten i Ukraina. Insatsen &#xe4;r &#xe4;ven relevant f&#xf6;r rapportering i f&#xf6;rh&#xe5;llande till den humanit&#xe4;ra situationen i Ukraina.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention aims to support OSCE in deploying international      observers in Ukraine. The special monitoring mission aims to reduce   the tensions in the eastern regions of Ukraine, reducing tensions and fostering peace stability and security.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this contribution was to allow FBA to deploy additional Swedish monitors as part of the OSCE Special Monitoring Mission (OSCE SMM) in Eastern Ukraine.
Sweden had been supporting OSCE monitors since 2014, however in 2015 there was a need for the monitoring capacity to be scaled up.
Therefore this contribution was meant to allow for an additional 4 monitors to be deployed for 15 months from 2015 onwards.
The long-term outcome of the intervention was &apos;stability and security in Ukraine based on the respect for human rights and fundamental freedoms including the rights of minorities&apos;.
The medium-term outcome was &apos;reduced tensions and stability throughout the country&apos;.</narrative>
  </description>
